WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.952 --> 00:00:05.270
(lively music)

00:00:08.062 --> 00:00:10.035
- We're in Inglewood, California.

00:00:10.035 --> 00:00:12.799
We're gonna eat a bunch
of vegan soul food.

00:00:12.799 --> 00:00:15.074
- Let me tell you somethin'
about soul food, okay.

00:00:15.074 --> 00:00:17.814
- So Daisha here, is in
another video right now.

00:00:17.814 --> 00:00:20.252
She's doing a 30 day vegan food challenge.

00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:21.808
- What do I know about soul food?

00:00:21.808 --> 00:00:23.201
I think mac and cheese.

00:00:23.201 --> 00:00:24.594
I think fried chicken.

00:00:24.594 --> 00:00:26.266
I think cornbread.

00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:27.700
(lively music)

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.949
- Inglewood, like many low income areas

00:00:34.949 --> 00:00:36.459
of Los Angeles, really struggles

00:00:36.459 --> 00:00:38.804
to feed people quality, healthy foods.

00:00:38.804 --> 00:00:42.054
- Oh, welcome to Stuff I Eat.

00:00:42.054 --> 00:00:44.191
- Babette opened this restaurant in 2008

00:00:44.191 --> 00:00:45.677
to try and combat that issue.

00:00:45.677 --> 00:00:47.070
She's inspiring the community

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.067
to understand food they love

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.622
in a broader context.

00:00:50.622 --> 00:00:51.574
- I think we should put it on you

00:00:51.574 --> 00:00:52.805
to come up with a rubric.

00:00:52.805 --> 00:00:54.128
- This is all based around a party

00:00:54.128 --> 00:00:55.336
in your mouth, all right?

00:00:55.336 --> 00:00:57.263
So the first thing is a Shindig.

00:00:57.263 --> 00:00:58.958
If things are, "Oh wow, this is great."

00:00:58.958 --> 00:01:00.792
"I'd probably eat this on my own time,

00:01:00.792 --> 00:01:02.301
"but I'm not, like, in love,"

00:01:02.301 --> 00:01:03.532
that is a Kickback.

00:01:03.532 --> 00:01:04.577
Then the next level up

00:01:04.577 --> 00:01:05.645
is a House Party.

00:01:05.645 --> 00:01:06.388
- House party.

00:01:06.388 --> 00:01:07.595
- All right, house party.

00:01:07.595 --> 00:01:09.801
And then if we are just completely,

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.055
completely blown away,

00:01:11.055 --> 00:01:12.471
all it is is just a Rave.

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:13.516
(beeping)

00:01:13.516 --> 00:01:15.513
- So is this your very first soul food,

00:01:15.513 --> 00:01:16.976
vegan soul food platter?

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.067
Really?

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.391
So first of all, let me describe

00:01:19.391 --> 00:01:21.271
exactly what you have on this plate.

00:01:21.271 --> 00:01:22.061
- [Daisha] This is vegan?

00:01:22.061 --> 00:01:24.568
- This is all vegan, 100% vegan.

00:01:24.568 --> 00:01:28.191
Kale greens, black-eyed peas.

00:01:28.191 --> 00:01:29.746
We've got mac and cheese.

00:01:29.746 --> 00:01:30.489
- [Voiceover] Vegan.

00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:31.650
- Vegan.

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.322
Barbecue tofu.

00:01:33.322 --> 00:01:34.669
Get a little coleslaw

00:01:34.669 --> 00:01:36.805
and potato salad.

00:01:36.805 --> 00:01:39.986
You've got some gluten-free cornbread

00:01:39.986 --> 00:01:40.961
and your yams.

00:01:40.961 --> 00:01:43.799
- Ready, go!

00:01:44.699 --> 00:01:46.116
- [Voiceover] Collin,
you're an animal Collin.

00:01:46.116 --> 00:01:47.437
- [Collin] I am an animal.

00:01:47.927 --> 00:01:49.222
(lively music)

00:01:50.086 --> 00:01:51.294
- Yes.

00:01:51.294 --> 00:01:52.454
Oh my God.

00:01:52.454 --> 00:01:53.824
This mac and cheese is so good.

00:01:53.824 --> 00:01:55.914
- Yeah, I wouldn't say it tastes like,

00:01:55.914 --> 00:01:57.470
you know, like traditional mac and cheese.

00:01:57.470 --> 00:02:00.411
- She's not trying to imitate

00:02:00.411 --> 00:02:01.765
regular soul food mac and cheese.

00:02:01.765 --> 00:02:02.857
She's, like, made it her own

00:02:02.857 --> 00:02:04.227
and it's amazing.

00:02:04.227 --> 00:02:05.875
- Everyday, I'd eat this everyday.

00:02:05.875 --> 00:02:08.165
- The mac and cheese is
a House Party for me.

00:02:08.685 --> 00:02:10.464
- I think this is a House Party for tofu.

00:02:10.914 --> 00:02:12.562
- I've never had tofu before.

00:02:12.562 --> 00:02:14.605
- What?
- Like, I've never had tofu.

00:02:14.605 --> 00:02:16.455
In my mind, it's always been like,

00:02:17.345 --> 00:02:18.135
- [Voiceover] Weird.

00:02:18.135 --> 00:02:19.644
- scary and weird, yeah.

00:02:19.644 --> 00:02:20.875
- Did y'all have this coleslaw?

00:02:20.875 --> 00:02:21.803
This is a Rave.

00:02:21.803 --> 00:02:23.429
- The coleslaw's amazing
- The coleslaw's a Rave.

00:02:23.429 --> 00:02:25.217
(beeping)

00:02:25.217 --> 00:02:28.862
- [Voiceover] Daisha, Daisha
(unintelligible) eat right.

00:02:28.862 --> 00:02:29.698
Steven.

00:02:29.698 --> 00:02:32.345
- My plate, almost done.

00:02:32.345 --> 00:02:34.760
- [Voiceover] Freddy,
pick up the pace, Freddy.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.524
- I'm comin', I'm comin', I'm comin'.

00:02:36.524 --> 00:02:38.242
- What's your definition of, like,

00:02:38.242 --> 00:02:39.562
a balanced meal?

00:02:40.262 --> 00:02:41.075
- That.

00:02:41.075 --> 00:02:41.748
- This?

00:02:41.748 --> 00:02:43.977
- What did you expect
me to say? (laughing)

00:02:43.977 --> 00:02:45.812
So when we first moved over here,

00:02:45.812 --> 00:02:47.623
I introduced the Soul Food Platter.

00:02:47.623 --> 00:02:49.829
It was only going to be a special.

00:02:49.829 --> 00:02:52.034
A couple of the local residents came in.

00:02:52.034 --> 00:02:53.172
They had the Soul Food Platter

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.496
and they liked it

00:02:54.496 --> 00:02:57.677
and then I didn't have
it, like, the next day.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:59.813
And they were like, "Well,
what happened to that?"

00:02:59.813 --> 00:03:01.647
And I'm like, "Well,
it was just a special."

00:03:01.647 --> 00:03:02.620
They walked out.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:05.246
That happened several times,

00:03:05.246 --> 00:03:06.477
several weeks in a row

00:03:06.477 --> 00:03:08.125
and we just made the Soul Food Platter

00:03:08.125 --> 00:03:09.518
a part of the menu

00:03:09.518 --> 00:03:10.354
and I think that's how

00:03:10.354 --> 00:03:13.628
we became the vegan soul food restaurant.

00:03:13.628 --> 00:03:14.998
- Why did you want to open in Inglewood?

00:03:14.998 --> 00:03:16.566
- I live down the street.

00:03:17.256 --> 00:03:20.594
First of all, every time I wanted a decent

00:03:20.594 --> 00:03:23.218
vegan meal, I had to drive across town.

00:03:23.218 --> 00:03:25.261
There are a lot of health conscious people

00:03:25.261 --> 00:03:26.863
living in this community.

00:03:26.863 --> 00:03:28.813
The rent was amazing.

00:03:28.813 --> 00:03:31.367
I'm not paying $20,000 a month for rent.

00:03:31.367 --> 00:03:33.248
Miss me Beverly Hills.

00:03:33.248 --> 00:03:34.734
And they needed me here.

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:36.661
They needed this situated right here

00:03:36.661 --> 00:03:38.194
where it is and why not?

00:03:38.194 --> 00:03:40.539
Why not a good vegan restuaruant

00:03:40.539 --> 00:03:42.016
in my community?

00:03:42.396 --> 00:03:43.627
- So since you've been here,

00:03:43.627 --> 00:03:44.834
have you noticed that more people

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:46.297
from the neighborhood
have started to come?

00:03:46.297 --> 00:03:47.667
- Oh definitely.
- Like people who aren't vegan

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:48.758
who just come for the food?

00:03:48.758 --> 00:03:50.779
- Most of my customers are not vegan.

00:03:50.779 --> 00:03:54.726
I'm so grateful that I was introduced

00:03:54.726 --> 00:03:56.699
to this lifestyle and made the transition.

00:03:56.699 --> 00:03:58.000
I really am.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.447
I started at age 40.

00:04:00.447 --> 00:04:02.806
I'll be 65 in December.

00:04:02.806 --> 00:04:05.732
I can still jump down and do my push ups.

00:04:05.732 --> 00:04:07.844
I'm still running hills.

00:04:07.844 --> 00:04:09.679
I'm not on medication.

00:04:09.679 --> 00:04:10.909
- [Voiceover] Your life
is (unintelligible)

00:04:10.909 --> 00:04:12.094
- My life is (laughing)

00:04:12.094 --> 00:04:14.462
my life is wonderful right now.

00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:16.598
- You know I've never for one second

00:04:16.598 --> 00:04:18.154
thought about becoming vegan,

00:04:18.154 --> 00:04:21.079
but I'm actually legitimately
considering it now.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:22.635
Like, with how good the food is

00:04:22.635 --> 00:04:23.958
and how good you look.

00:04:23.958 --> 00:04:25.096
(laughing)

00:04:25.096 --> 00:04:26.350
- If I could just say one thing,

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.045
if there are any kids out there

00:04:28.045 --> 00:04:30.297
eating those spicy Cheetos,

00:04:30.297 --> 00:04:32.039
maybe you shouldn't eat those things

00:04:32.039 --> 00:04:33.130
and that's all I have to say

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:34.523
about spicy Cheetos.

00:04:34.523 --> 00:04:37.165
I know we're not talking
about spicy Cheetos.

